# rarpar License

rarpar is licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later with the additional UnRAR
source-code restriction reproduced at the end of this file.

The restriction is not a property of only the binaries. `unrar-rs` is a
default dependency of this crate: it is pulled in by the `runtime` feature,
and `default = ["runtime", "musl-allocator"]`. An ordinary `cargo build`,
`cargo install` or release archive therefore contains UnRAR-derived RAR
extraction and recovery code and carries the restriction with it.

Only a deliberate `--no-default-features` build that also omits `runtime`
links no `unrar-rs`. That configuration is GPL-3.0-or-later alone, and it is
not what any distributed rarpar is — so rarpar is described as
GPL-3.0-or-later AND the UnRAR restriction, rather than as GPL-3.0-or-later
with a caveat about binaries.

Binary release archives include:

- `LICENSE`: this rarpar license notice.
- `LICENSE.GPL-3.0-or-later`: the full GNU GPL version 3 text.
- `LICENSE.unrar-rs`: the complete unrar-rs license text, including
  the UnRAR source-code restriction.

Source checkouts include the full GNU GPL version 3 text in the workspace root
`LICENSE` file and the complete unrar-rs license in
`crates/unrar-rs/LICENSE`.

## UnRAR Source-Code Restriction

UnRAR source code may be used in any software to handle
RAR archives without limitations free of charge, but cannot be
used to develop RAR (WinRAR) compatible archiver and to
re-create RAR compression algorithm, which is proprietary.
Distribution of modified UnRAR source code in separate form
or as a part of other software is permitted, provided that
full text of this paragraph, starting from "UnRAR source code"
words, is included in license, or in documentation if license
is not available, and in source code comments of resulting package.
